feat(ui): iOS tab order: Contacts, Chats, Settings

DESIGN_SPEC section 7. iOS Telegram shows Contacts, Chats and Settings
(Calls is an optional extra tab) and has no Profile tab.

- MainTabsActivity: Contacts is the first tab and page, Chats the second,
  Settings the third. Chats stays selected at start and is still the
  target of the back button. The Calls and Profile tabs are still
  created but hidden, so the upstream logic around them keeps working;
  the pager has 3 pages. The account-switch hint that points at the
  hidden Profile tab is not shown.
- SettingsActivity: new "Recent Calls" row (as on iOS), because the
  Calls tab is gone. Recent calls also stay in the Contacts tab menu.
  Other accounts are already listed in Settings.

One switch, MYCLIENT_IOS_TABS in MainTabsActivity, turns the upstream
layout back on.
